    "created_at": "2018-04-05T07:08:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-05T07:08:20Z",
    "body": "> So every browser excludes Edge?\r\n\r\nEdge has it, and so does IE9 ... but they have non de-facto standard behavior (which is why I'd like this to be standardized and we can fix those)\r\n\r\n> Would you mind filing an issue against that specification?\r\n\r\nSure thing. Where should I do that?\r\n\r\n> HTML should probably not also start defining mouse events.\r\n\r\nTo be clear, this is not strictly a mouse event. Pointer events expose layerX too as well as touches so I'm not fully sure where this should go (although UIEvent sounds right as meta group)\r\n\r\n",
